# Review: GitHub polling sync

Part 1 is implemented and tested closely against the spec. `syncRepoBinding` sends one conditional
`listIssuesSince` per poll, batches pull requests (plus pending ones, and every open one on the hourly
read) into `fetchPullRequestDetails`, merges issues three ways, backfills oldest first in 10-page chunks,
and advances `Cursor.max` to the newest `updated_at` minus 5 s only after every page. `sync-poll.test.ts`
runs T-1, T-2, T-3, T-5, T-6 and T-7 against a fake GitHub (its test named "T-4" is really T-7). Gaps:
the `SyncGitHubRepositories` input has no `binding` field (it takes the shared `SyncInput`, with
`priority` only); spec T-4 (import of a synced pull request) has no test; and `useSyncPullRequest`
refreshes on open in every space, bound or not.

Of 33 items: 26 done, 3 untested, 3 partial, 0 diverged, 1 missing.

